=== 4. coefficient equations ===
  [u^0] coefficient: a**2 + b**2*dbar*m0  | minus claimed: 0
  [u^1] coefficient: a**2*dbar + 2*a*b + b**2*dbar*m1 - d*kp  | minus claimed: 0
  [u^2] coefficient: 2*a*b*dbar + b**2*dbar*m2 + b**2 - kp  | minus claimed: 0
  [u] after a = lam b and kp from [u^2]: -d*dbar*m2 - d + dbar*lam**2 + dbar*m1 + lam*(-2*d*dbar + 2)   (quadratic in lam: needs [1] to linearise)
  lambda from [u] with lam^2 = -dbar m0: (-d*dbar*m2 - d - dbar**2*m0 + dbar*m1)/(2*(d*dbar - 1)) ; minus THM/script formula: 0
=== 5. minimal polynomial of u over Q(j) ===
  cubic in h = w + 3: h**3 - 7*h**2 + 11*h - 1
  monic cubic: U^3 + (11*j/19 + 20/19) U^2 + (11*j/19 - 20/19) U + (-1)
  u^3 = m2 u^2 + m1 u + m0 with m2 = -11*j/19 - 20/19 , m1 = 20/19 - 11*j/19 , m0 = 1
  equals THM values (m2 = -(20+11j)/19, m1 = (20-11j)/19, m0 = 1): True True True
  factorisation over Q(sqrt(-11)): [(3, 1)]
  w = 1.70927535943692283922913166712 ; |u^3 - m2 u^2 - m1 u - 1| at the embedding (50 digits): 2.6728e-51
=== 6. field degrees ===
  Phi_15 over Q(sqrt(-11)) factor degrees: [8] => [K:Q] = 16
  primes p = 1 mod 15 with (-11/p) = 1 (split completely in K) where w^3+2w^2-4w-4 has NO root mod p: [181, 751, 1291]
  => the monic integral cubic has no root in K (a root would be integral in K and reduce to F_p), so [F:K] = 3, [F:Q] = 48
  disc of the cubic over Q: 592 {2: 4, 37: 1} (not a square: S3 cubic, three real roots)
